      ],
      "margin_number": 186,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "The optative forms are used with the particle ἄν to express a ‘polite’ request\nor agreement. Sometimes ‘polite’ requests are difficult to distinguish from\nstraightforward requests. The best translations involve using the English\nforms ‘would’, ‘would like to’, ‘can’, or the simple future ‘will’, e.g.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 1,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        652,
        238,
        689,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "λέγοις ἄν μοι; ‘Would you tell me? Would you like to/could you/will\nyou tell me?’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "bullet",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
